# Client stub for the Unified Service Scheduler (VS Code REST Client, JetBrains HTTP client, or Visual Studio).
# Start the stack first: docker compose -f deploy/docker-compose.yml up --build
# Demo data: dealership 1 "Thames Valley Motors" (Europe/London, Mon–Sat 08:00–18:00) has 3 bays.

@host = http://localhost:8080
@day = 2027-03-04

### 1. Book an oil change at 09:00 London time → 201 with technician and bay
POST {{host}}/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dealershipId": 1,
  "serviceType": "OIL",
  "start": "{{day}}T09:00:00+00:00",
  "customer": { "name": "Ava Thompson", "email": "ava.thompson@example.com" },
  "vehicle": { "vin": "WVWZZZ1KZAW000001", "make": "Volkswagen", "model": "Golf" }
}

### 2. Same slot, same Idempotency-Key, sent twice → the same appointment both times
POST {{host}}/appointments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-booking-42

{
  "dealershipId": 1,
  "serviceType": "OIL",
  "start": "{{day}}T09:00:00+00:00",
  "customer": { "name": "Ben Carter", "email": "ben.carter@example.com" },
  "vehicle": { "vin": "WVWZZZ1KZAW000002", "make": "Volkswagen", "model": "Polo" }
}

### 3. A third booking at 09:00 fills the last of the 3 bays → 201
POST {{host}}/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dealershipId": 1,
  "serviceType": "OIL",
  "start": "{{day}}T09:00:00+00:00",
  "customer": { "name": "Chloe Patel", "email": "chloe.patel@example.com" },
  "vehicle": { "vin": "SAJAA06E0EP000003", "make": "Jaguar", "model": "XF" }
}

### 4. A fourth at 09:00 → 409 Conflict, outcome "NoCapacity"
POST {{host}}/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dealershipId": 1,
  "serviceType": "OIL",
  "start": "{{day}}T09:00:00+00:00",
  "customer": { "name": "Dan Murphy", "email": "dan.murphy@example.com" },
  "vehicle": { "vin": "WBA3A5C50DF000004", "make": "BMW", "model": "320d" }
}

### 5. EV work needs the "ev" skill: only Priya Shah (103) qualifies → 201 with technician 103
POST {{host}}/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dealershipId": 1,
  "serviceType": "EV-BATT",
  "start": "{{day}}T13:00:00+00:00",
  "customer": { "name": "Ella Novak", "email": "ella.novak@example.com" },
  "vehicle": { "vin": "5YJ3E1EA7KF000005", "make": "Tesla", "model": "Model 3" }
}

### 6. Don't wait for the decision → 202 Accepted with a Location to poll
# @name async
POST {{host}}/appointments
Content-Type: application/json
Prefer: respond-async

{
  "dealershipId": 1,
  "serviceType": "BRAKES",
  "start": "{{day}}T15:00:00+00:00",
  "customer": { "name": "Finn Walsh", "email": "finn.walsh@example.com" },
  "vehicle": { "vin": "VF1RFB00X5Y000006", "make": "Renault", "model": "Clio" }
}

### 7. Poll the request from step 6 → "confirmed" with its appointment id
GET {{host}}{{async.response.headers.Location}}

### 8. Get a confirmed appointment (use an id from a 201 above)
GET {{host}}/appointments/1

### 9. Free start times for an oil change that day (read model: 09:00 disappears shortly after steps 1–3)
GET {{host}}/availability?dealershipId=1&serviceType=OIL&date={{day}}

### 10. After closing (17:30 + 60 min > 18:00) → 422, outcome "OutsideOpeningHours"
POST {{host}}/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dealershipId": 1,
  "serviceType": "OIL",
  "start": "{{day}}T17:30:00+00:00",
  "customer": { "name": "Gia Rossi", "email": "gia.rossi@example.com" },
  "vehicle": { "vin": "ZFA31200000000007", "make": "Fiat", "model": "500" }
}

### 11. Malformed input → 400 ValidationProblem keyed by field ("vehicle.vin", "customer.email")
POST {{host}}/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dealershipId": 1,
  "serviceType": "OIL",
  "start": "{{day}}T10:00:00+00:00",
  "customer": { "name": "Bad Input", "email": "not-an-email" },
  "vehicle": { "vin": "TOO-SHORT", "make": "Ford", "model": "Focus" }
}

### 12. The API contract
GET {{host}}/openapi/v1.json
